INT: How did you to get on that ship? Who led you?

EM: This was a organization. It was a--

INT: What organization was it?

EM: The organization who helped me out, it was the IRC. That was a Rescue Committee, International Rescue Committee.

INT: How long was it till your parents came from when you got to Camp Kilmer? You said, you left in 1957, and they left in 1957.

EM: They went to Austria.

INT: But how long in between did you get reunited?

EM: Well, it was a year or so. It was a year.

INT: Where did you--

EM: Because they came in 1958, yeah.

INT: Where did you go when you arrived in the United States? Beside--

EM: Camp Kilmer.

INT: But where did you go from there?

EM: From there, I went to my uncle's house in Long Island, New York.

INT: What was your uncle's name that sponsored you?

EM: Kenneth K. Scott. Scott-- Kenneth K. Scott. Otherwise, his name was Schwarcz in Hungarian. But he picked up the English version. So he was--

INT: What was his last name?

EM: In English or Hungarian?

INT: In English, his last name.

EM: Scott.

INT: Scott?

EM: Yeah.

INT: S-C-O-T-T?

EM: Mm-hmm.

INT: So your first impressions were you were free. [PAUSES] And it's 1957.

EM: Seven.

INT: So you're how old?

EM: Actually, not. In 1956, because I was in already in-- free in Austria--

INT: Right.

EM: --before I came here.

INT: So your first impressions beside being free?

EM: It was wonderful, like a free bird.

INT: And what did you do when you got here?

EM: Well, I went to his home. And I got sick right away. I got the measles.

INT: Yeah, you mentioned that.

EM: And I was sick for 10 days. And he brought in to the doctor, to the-- you know, at that time, the doctors make house calls. And he came. And I think so he gave me some kind of medication. But my uncle said to me, you know, that cost me $10 to come here. And it's expensive. I said, I can't help it. And I got sick. I was probably-- I brought that germ from the ship. Because I was there in 11 days. And it was children and parents and grandparents. It was all kind of people who was able to, you know, escape and be a refugee. And after that, he took me to the city, to New York, and brought me into the-- [PAUSES] how you call that agency where provide you jobs?

